      },
      {
        "id": "n10_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          840
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 1 \u00b7 Bars\n\nThree columns is all it takes: **Task**, **Duration** and **Depends on**.\n\nEvery task here waits for another one, so only *Kickoff workshop* has nothing\nin front of it \u2014 and its date comes from **Project start**, not from the\ntable. Every other date is worked out by following the chain.\n\n**Depends on** holds ids from the **Task id** column, comma separated where a\ntask waits for two. *Requirements agreed* waits for both the interviews and\nthe audit, so it starts when the later of the two ends.\n\n**Calendar** is set to working days, so the bars step over weekends. Switch it\nto calendar days and watch the plan close up by a fortnight.",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 300
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "n11_from",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
        "pos": [
          700,
          960
        ],
        "params": {
          "source": "n02_goto"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Task list"
      },
      {
        "id": "n12_gantt",
        "type": "flograph.viz.gantt",
        "pos": [
          1120,
          700
        ],
        "params": {
          "task": "task",
          "task_id": "id",
          "duration": "duration",
          "depends_on": "depends_on",
          "project_start": "2026-09-07",
          "calendar": "working days (Mon-Fri)",
          "show_dependencies": false,
          "width": 720,
          "height": 560,
          "title": "Website Rebuild \u2014 bars"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "1 \u00b7 Gantt",
        "preview": false
      },
      {
        "id": "n20_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          1680
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 2 \u00b7 Phases and progress\n\nTwo more columns, and the same chart starts to read like a plan.\n\n**Group by** blocks the tasks under a heading and tints alternate phases, so\nDiscovery, Design and Build read as three bands rather than fourteen bars.\n\n**Color by** is a separate setting on purpose. It follows the grouping column\nunless you tell it otherwise \u2014 point it at **owner** instead and the chart\nanswers \"who is doing what?\" without giving up the phases. Try it.\n\n**Progress** shades the finished part of each bar. It takes 0\u2013100 or 0\u20131;\nthis table is in percentages.",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 280
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "n21_from",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
        "pos": [
          700,
          1800
        ],
        "params": {
          "source": "n02_goto"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Task list"
      },
      {
        "id": "n22_gantt",
        "type": "flograph.viz.gantt",
        "pos": [
          1120,
          1540
        ],
        "params": {
          "task": "task",
          "task_id": "id",
          "duration": "duration",
          "depends_on": "depends_on",
          "project_start": "2026-09-07",
          "calendar": "working days (Mon-Fri)",
          "show_dependencies": false,
          "width": 720,
          "height": 560,
          "title": "Website Rebuild \u2014 phases and progress",
          "group": "phase",
          "progress": "progress"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "2 \u00b7 Gantt",
        "preview": false
      },
      {
        "id": "n30_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          2520
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 3 \u00b7 Dependencies and milestones\n\n**Show dependencies** draws the links that were there all along. The node has\nbeen scheduling from them since stage 1 \u2014 now you can see them, each arrow\ndropping from the end of one bar to the start of the next.\n\nLook at *Requirements agreed* and *Design signed off*: they are **diamonds,\nnot bars**, because their duration is **0**. That is all it takes to put a\nmilestone on a chart, and two arrows arrive at each \u2014 one per predecessor.\n\nFollow the arrows out of *Design signed off* and two tasks start at once.\n*Page templates* is the longer of the pair, so everything after it is really\nwaiting on that one.",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 280
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "n31_from",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
        "pos": [
          700,
          2640
        ],
        "params": {
          "source": "n02_goto"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Task list"
      },
      {
        "id": "n32_gantt",
        "type": "flograph.viz.gantt",
        "pos": [
          1120,
          2380
        ],
        "params": {
          "task": "task",
          "task_id": "id",
          "duration": "duration",
          "depends_on": "depends_on",
          "project_start": "2026-09-07",
          "calendar": "working days (Mon-Fri)",
          "show_dependencies": true,
          "width": 720,
          "height": 560,
          "title": "Website Rebuild \u2014 dependencies",
          "group": "phase",
          "progress": "progress"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "3 \u00b7 Gantt",
        "preview": false
      },
      {
        "id": "n40_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          3280
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 4 \u00b7 What you promised, and what happened\n\n**Show baseline** adds the thin grey bar under each task: the dates this\nproject was originally sold on. Where grey runs past colour, the task is\nlate \u2014 by *Go live* the plan has slipped over a week. Hover a grey bar and it\nsays how far.\n\nThe node's second output, **schedule**, is the table on the right: the dates\nit worked out, as ordinary data. Wire it into a filter, a chart or a Write\nExcel like anything else.\n\nThe third, **html**, is the chart as a standalone web page. Tick **Emit\nHTML**, wire it into a **Write Text** node, and you have a file to send\nsomeone who has no flograph \u2014 plotly.js travels inside it, so it opens with\nno internet. It is off by default because that page is around 4.5 MB.\n\n### Try it\n\nOpen the **Website Rebuild** table and change *Page templates* from 8 days to\n13. Run the flow. Every task after it moves, both milestones move, Go live\nlands a fortnight later \u2014 and the grey baseline stays exactly where it was,\nwhich is the whole point of having one.",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 440
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "n41_from",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
